WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.890
- Aight y'all, y'all ready for the show?

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.396
(drumming)

00:00:04.396 --> 00:00:06.749
- When you’re on the stage and
you're giving it your all

00:00:06.749 --> 00:00:08.586
and the show comes to an end

00:00:08.586 --> 00:00:11.467
and you know that you've
left everything on that stage.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.538
That is the most rewarding feeling.

00:00:13.538 --> 00:00:17.287
(powerful drumming music)

00:00:17.287 --> 00:00:20.370
(audience cheering)

00:00:23.344 --> 00:00:24.557
I am Byron Hannah.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.809
The step master of the Sigmas
here at North Carolina A&amp;T.

00:00:27.809 --> 00:00:29.773
To be the step master is to be that person

00:00:29.773 --> 00:00:31.787
that creates the steps,

00:00:31.787 --> 00:00:33.131
bring it back to the team

00:00:33.131 --> 00:00:36.881
and teach everyone how to do these steps.

00:00:36.881 --> 00:00:38.334
Stepping is a combination of clapping

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:40.502
and stomping in a particular rhythm.

00:00:40.502 --> 00:00:42.669
It comes from Africa.

00:00:42.669 --> 00:00:45.208
Stepping serves a huge
role in historically black

00:00:45.208 --> 00:00:46.937
Greek organizations.

00:00:46.937 --> 00:00:50.493
And these organizations were
founded in the early 1900s.

00:00:50.493 --> 00:00:52.647
They were put together
to make a more powerful

00:00:52.647 --> 00:00:54.421
force in the community.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.348
Stepping is something that
fraternities and sororities

00:00:56.348 --> 00:00:58.740
brought to the current day.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.056
- [Announcer] Y'all
ready for the grand show,

00:01:00.056 --> 00:01:01.213
make some noise!

00:01:01.213 --> 00:01:04.243
(audience cheering)

00:01:04.243 --> 00:01:06.699
- Steps are always one of
the main events at GHOE,

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.335
which stands for the
Greatest Homecoming On Earth.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.396
It brings in thousands
and thousands of people.

00:01:11.396 --> 00:01:15.189
We have been winning the step
show for 11 years straight.

00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:17.729
When fraternities and
sororities go on the stage,

00:01:17.729 --> 00:01:19.658
there is so much to lose.

00:01:19.658 --> 00:01:21.960
Reputation, respect.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.656
So the pressure for the Sigmas winning

00:01:24.656 --> 00:01:27.156
11 consecutive years is crazy.

00:01:29.359 --> 00:01:31.778
You know where you need to be.

00:01:31.778 --> 00:01:33.046
You gotta come back, right.

00:01:33.046 --> 00:01:35.744
As the step master, I serve as the coach.

00:01:35.744 --> 00:01:38.172
The captain, team member.

00:01:38.172 --> 00:01:39.538
All these things in one person.

00:01:39.538 --> 00:01:41.916
The biggest pressure that is on my back

00:01:41.916 --> 00:01:44.166
is maintaining that legacy.

00:01:45.097 --> 00:01:48.650
To become a good stepper
is very, very difficult.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.917
It's something that you really gotta give

00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:53.445
all your dedication to.

00:01:53.445 --> 00:01:56.155
To stomp so loud, clap so loud

00:01:56.155 --> 00:02:00.266
and scream so loud is an
opportunity to let loose.

00:02:00.266 --> 00:02:02.050
It's very, very therapeutic.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.624
That's why we usually do the face.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.026
It's a face of disgust.

00:02:06.026 --> 00:02:08.675
And we do that to push out more energy

00:02:08.675 --> 00:02:10.489
and push out more anger.

00:02:10.489 --> 00:02:14.318
You are destroying your
body on concrete pavement

00:02:14.318 --> 00:02:16.021
day in and day out for four months.

00:02:16.021 --> 00:02:18.921
On some nights, I walk away
from the practice limping.

00:02:18.921 --> 00:02:21.414
Sometimes we have the mentality that okay,

00:02:21.414 --> 00:02:23.911
we already won 11 years in a row

00:02:23.911 --> 00:02:26.628
so, you know, what's another year gonna do.

00:02:26.628 --> 00:02:28.085
But one thing that we have to keep in mind

00:02:28.085 --> 00:02:29.385
is that we can't lose.

00:02:29.385 --> 00:02:32.068
(clapping)

00:02:32.068 --> 00:02:34.750
(dramatic piano music)

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.685
So the night of the step show,

00:02:36.685 --> 00:02:37.678
being backstage,

00:02:37.678 --> 00:02:39.180
I feel like I'm ready for it.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.620
And I feel like my team is ready for it.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.164
A lot of older brothers come back there,

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.500
you know, giving encouraging words.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.285
- Let's close this show
out with excitement

00:02:47.285 --> 00:02:48.118
and with a bang.

00:02:48.118 --> 00:02:50.488
- When the timer's counting down,

00:02:50.488 --> 00:02:52.987
I had to go run off into the corner

00:02:52.987 --> 00:02:55.403
and actually had to cry.

00:02:55.403 --> 00:02:57.244
Those tears weren't sadness.

00:02:57.244 --> 00:02:58.577
Something that had to bring me back

00:02:58.577 --> 00:03:01.642
to where I was and prepare
me to go out on the stage.

00:03:01.642 --> 00:03:02.983
- [Announcer] Welcome to the stage

00:03:02.983 --> 00:03:05.233
Brothers of Phi Beta Sigma.

00:03:08.428 --> 00:03:11.761
(uplifting piano music)

00:03:13.141 --> 00:03:17.468
- I legit left everything
that I had on that stage.

00:03:17.468 --> 00:03:20.801
(clapping and stomping)

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.039
Push it guys, push it.

00:03:32.235 --> 00:03:35.235
(audience cheering)

00:03:36.636 --> 00:03:38.180
- My feet are on fire.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:42.632
- We are waiting on the judges
to calculate up the scores.

00:03:42.632 --> 00:03:46.366
Just to know that the legacy
is on the line right now.

00:03:46.366 --> 00:03:49.956
- [Announcer] Alright,
let's get to these winners.

00:03:49.956 --> 00:03:52.877
(clapping)

00:03:52.877 --> 00:03:56.210
First place, undefeated, Phi Beta Sigma!

00:04:03.512 --> 00:04:04.565
- We won.

00:04:04.565 --> 00:04:05.832
I'm proud of every single person

00:04:05.832 --> 00:04:07.550
'cause it's been a long journey.

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:10.300
And now they're part of a legacy.

